#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-kwin-settings: Hearth Settings' pages for what KWin does when Mantel runs on KWin (docs/KWIN-SETTINGS.md).

The settings live where KWin reads them, one home each: kwinrc (effects, desktops, tiling, edges, Xwayland, tearing),
kdeglobals [KDE] (animation speed), kaccessrc (sticky, slow and bounce keys, the visual bell), kwinrulesrc (window
rules), and KWin's own input settings (kcminputrc, written by KWin when Hearth sets a device's property over D-Bus).
The mouse and touchpad settings stay in Hearth's pointer.json (shared with labwc) and are put on KWin's devices.
Only the keys the person changes are written (hearth_kconfig), then KWin is asked to read its settings again
(org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure) and KDE's "config changed" signal is sent, so nothing needs a restart.

  hearth-kwin-settings status                 JSON: is Mantel on KWin (live), KWin's version, effects, switchers
  hearth-kwin-settings get                    JSON: the settings as KWin sees them (system defaults + yours)
  hearth-kwin-settings set FILE               stdin {group: {key: value or null}}: change these keys in FILE
  hearth-kwin-settings desktops               JSON: virtual desktops (id, name), rows
  hearth-kwin-settings desktops-set           stdin {"count": n, "names": {id: name}, "rows": n}
  hearth-kwin-settings outputs                JSON: screens (name, KWin's id for its tile layouts, size)
  hearth-kwin-settings tiles-set UUID NAME    stdin {"columns": [{"width": w, "rows": [h, ...]}], "padding": px}
  hearth-kwin-settings rules                  JSON: window rules (kwinrulesrc)
  hearth-kwin-settings rule-set               stdin {"id": id or "", "set": {key: value or null}}: makes or changes one
  hearth-kwin-settings rule-delete ID
  hearth-kwin-settings pick-window            JSON: the window the person clicks (KWin's queryWindowInfo)
  hearth-kwin-settings input                  JSON: KWin's input devices and their settings
  hearth-kwin-settings input-set SYSNAME      stdin {property: value}: a tablet's or touchscreen's setting
  hearth-kwin-settings pointer-apply          puts pointer.json (Settings › Mouse & touchpad) on KWin's devices
  hearth-kwin-settings input-watch            pointer-apply now and whenever a device is plugged in (session)
  hearth-kwin-settings rebind TOOL BUTTON     stdin action ("" = as it is): a pen button (kcminputrc ButtonRebinds)
  hearth-kwin-settings shortcut NAME          runs one of KWin's own shortcuts (zoom in, invert, overview...)

Preview (tests only): HEARTH_KWIN_FIXTURE=<json file> plus $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth-kwin-preview makes the pages
usable without KWin (devices, screens and effects from the file; nothing is sent to KWin).
"""
